  "old_string": "Jian et al. (2016, Space Weather, doi:10.1002/2016SW001435), as relayed by my validation sub-search **[UNVERIFIED by me]**: an ENLIL v2.8 alternative setting raises the B scaling factor 2 → 4 and lowers the inner-boundary fast-wind density 200 → 125 cm⁻³.",
  "new_string": "Jian et al. (2016, Space Weather, doi:10.1002/2016SW001435) **[text, read by me]**, author copy https://ips.ucsd.edu/ftp/pub/SCRPA_2019/111_Jian_et_al-2016-Space_Weather.pdf:\n- §1.3: Enlil v2.7 deliberately used a setting with weaker B and lower T \"to enhance system robustness\" (lower characteristic speeds at the inner boundary keep the outflow supercritical). Enlil v2.8 (CCMC, late 2015) has an \"increased magnetic field scaling factor and added heating.\"\n- §7: relative to the present setting (a4b1), the alternative setting decreases the number density \"from 200 to 125 cm⁻³\" and increases the B scaling factor \"from 2 to 4.\" This gives lower N_p and stronger B at Ulysses, with mixed overall effect.\n- Note: these ENLIL densities (125–200 cm⁻³) differ from the \"300\" in the MacNeice slide. Version and setting matter, and I could not confirm which quantity (fast-wind n at 21.5 R_s) each refers to **[UNVERIFIED]**."
}

